 ## Overview
-Inverse CDF Ray Sampling is a CUDA kernel that samples points along rays using inverse CDF sampling based on probability distributions (probs) associated with depth intervals (hits), supporting optional fixed step size [S1, unofficial]. It maps uniform random noise to depth intervals using the cumulative distribution function derived from per-hit probabilities [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Near-Far Linear Ray Generation](6841-near-far-linear-ray-generation.md) by replacing uniform spacing with probability-weighted stratification.
+Inverse CDF Ray Sampling is a CUDA kernel that samples points along rays using inverse CDF sampling based on probability distributions (probs) associated with depth intervals (hits), supporting optional fixed step size [S1, unofficial]. It maps uniform random noise to depth intervals using the cumulative distribution function derived from per-hit probabilities [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Near-Far Linear Ray Generation](6841-near-far-linear-ray-generation.md) by replacing uniform spacing with probability-weighted stratification [G].
 
